    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense. If the binder is becoming that brittle so quickly, I'm worried there might be some localized failures happening under the surface that we aren't seeing immediately. In your experience, are there any specific indicators in the subgrade or the mix design that would suggest the material is failing prematurely from the inside out, or is it strictly just a surface-level aging issue?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
